[{:db/id "c7f9650f-e3d4-52e1-8604-95b13a333df9" :answer/id #uuid "c7f9650f-e3d4-52e1-8604-95b13a333df9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{8}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5352939e-cae2-5159-bff4-104d22d61c5b" :answer/id #uuid "5352939e-cae2-5159-bff4-104d22d61c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "78f292e0-a2c7-5fcd-8ee3-576f77b454aa" :answer/id #uuid "78f292e0-a2c7-5fcd-8ee3-576f77b454aa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1000$ percent per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f26ac375-519e-5368-9853-c2be81821dcc" :answer/id #uuid "f26ac375-519e-5368-9853-c2be81821dcc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{25}$ percent per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d1a55db6-62c2-5bd7-ba6f-3238abbd84a1" :answer/id #uuid "d1a55db6-62c2-5bd7-ba6f-3238abbd84a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$100$ percent per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cac29cb1-6d21-5053-bb45-5161878e9c39" :answer-field/id #uuid "cac29cb1-6d21-5053-bb45-5161878e9c39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c7f9650f-e3d4-52e1-8604-95b13a333df9" "5352939e-cae2-5159-bff4-104d22d61c5b" "78f292e0-a2c7-5fcd-8ee3-576f77b454aa" "f26ac375-519e-5368-9853-c2be81821dcc" "d1a55db6-62c2-5bd7-ba6f-3238abbd84a1"] :answer-field/correct "f26ac375-519e-5368-9853-c2be81821dcc" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a5c334a0-b9d7-58f1-b30e-102327fa70dc" :question/id #uuid "a5c334a0-b9d7-58f1-b30e-102327fa70dc" :question/problem "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.4t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $10$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $10$ hours, we have $t=10.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $10$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(10) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.4(10)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{625} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $\\frac{4}{25}$ percent per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["cac29cb1-6d21-5053-bb45-5161878e9c39"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f" :answer/id #uuid "78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1/60" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "aef7959b-ba6c-5639-93da-84cf1b9feb78" :answer-field/id #uuid "aef7959b-ba6c-5639-93da-84cf1b9feb78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f"] :answer-field/correct "78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "631f3d25-1539-5b45-a5e3-359eb72f3729" :question/id #uuid "631f3d25-1539-5b45-a5e3-359eb72f3729" :question/problem "The supplied rate function is $h'(x)=\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{x}}$ thousand dollars per week, for $x>0$.\n\nWhat was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $144?$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ thousand dollars per week." :question/worked-solution "The function ${h}^{'}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $h(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=144$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{'}(144) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{60}$ thousand dollars per week." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["aef7959b-ba6c-5639-93da-84cf1b9feb78"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" :answer/id #uuid "89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8$ crocodiles per year" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2e530fff-ce9c-5970-b878-96dbbaeec603" :answer/id #uuid "2e530fff-ce9c-5970-b878-96dbbaeec603" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-8$ crocodiles per year" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f373a41d-03e8-5f52-b12e-d904b52de946" :answer/id #uuid "f373a41d-03e8-5f52-b12e-d904b52de946" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-3$ crocodiles per year" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "049a0fe5-6a20-5d0a-ade6-b497853f1f57" :answer/id #uuid "049a0fe5-6a20-5d0a-ade6-b497853f1f57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$14$ crocodiles per year" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9759bafc-fb74-5017-91e8-ab74ae726c77" :answer/id #uuid "9759bafc-fb74-5017-91e8-ab74ae726c77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$11$ crocodiles per year" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "13f111bb-5884-576a-a701-a9d50261c695" :answer-field/id #uuid "13f111bb-5884-576a-a701-a9d50261c695" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" "2e530fff-ce9c-5970-b878-96dbbaeec603" "f373a41d-03e8-5f52-b12e-d904b52de946" "049a0fe5-6a20-5d0a-ade6-b497853f1f57" "9759bafc-fb74-5017-91e8-ab74ae726c77"] :answer-field/correct "89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "43cee7e4-6ff9-5eeb-9102-bb7cf335c204" :question/id #uuid "43cee7e4-6ff9-5eeb-9102-bb7cf335c204" :question/problem "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t) = 4 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t) = 1 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000$.\n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2004$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the crocodile population is the birth rate minus the death rate.\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2004$ is $4$ years after $2000$, substitute $t=4$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(4)-D(4) & =4\\cdot e^{0.25(4)}-1\\cdot e^{0.25(4)} \\\\  & =3\\cdot e^{1} \\\\  & \\approx 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $8$ crocodiles per year." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["13f111bb-5884-576a-a701-a9d50261c695"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "de87630c-5e9f-5b64-8432-c235e63365fd" :answer/id #uuid "de87630c-5e9f-5b64-8432-c235e63365fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$232$ liters per minute" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" :answer/id #uuid "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$216$ liters per minute" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f60db18e-606e-507e-a70a-222aab527053" :answer/id #uuid "f60db18e-606e-507e-a70a-222aab527053" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-216$ liters per minute" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "51c48530-c821-53d2-8682-e23e9308cc96" :answer/id #uuid "51c48530-c821-53d2-8682-e23e9308cc96" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$248$ liters per minute" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b0854dc4-f4cb-5adf-93b0-a9de2132efc8" :answer/id #uuid "b0854dc4-f4cb-5adf-93b0-a9de2132efc8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-16$ liters per minute" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d55f1a11-95b1-5a99-93e1-ed8950cd0df2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d55f1a11-95b1-5a99-93e1-ed8950cd0df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["de87630c-5e9f-5b64-8432-c235e63365fd" "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" "f60db18e-606e-507e-a70a-222aab527053" "51c48530-c821-53d2-8682-e23e9308cc96" "b0854dc4-f4cb-5adf-93b0-a9de2132efc8"] :answer-field/correct "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4064584b-a92b-5c2b-aee4-39b559d5a1a6" :question/id #uuid "4064584b-a92b-5c2b-aee4-39b559d5a1a6" :question/problem "The rate $F$ at which a swimming pool is being filled can be modeled as $F(t) = 4t^{2} - 3t$ liters per minute, where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled. The rate at which water is leaking from the pool can be modeled as $L(t) = \\frac{1}{4}t^{2}$ liters per minute, where $t$ is also the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of the volume of water in the pool $8$ minutes after the pool began to be filled?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the volume of water is the filling rate minus the leaking rate.\n\n$$\nF(t)-L(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=8$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8)-L(8) & =4(8)^{2}-3(8)-\\frac{1}{4}(8)^{2} \\\\  & =232-16 \\\\  & =216.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $216$ liters per minute." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["d55f1a11-95b1-5a99-93e1-ed8950cd0df2"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "fa9bf1a9-9ed3-510e-8652-4bea14db43c6" :answer/id #uuid "fa9bf1a9-9ed3-510e-8652-4bea14db43c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$124$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "08f23811-b1ee-5151-b6b6-f608a52a57d3" :answer/id #uuid "08f23811-b1ee-5151-b6b6-f608a52a57d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$76$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "87ffd388-fbdd-5be1-b220-e00d63314682" :answer/id #uuid "87ffd388-fbdd-5be1-b220-e00d63314682" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-100$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "90fa38bd-a1a3-5389-bd58-781b51e91810" :answer/id #uuid "90fa38bd-a1a3-5389-bd58-781b51e91810" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-76$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cf7e8946-b8bd-5c22-9ef3-b4fcc20d9ffb" :answer/id #uuid "cf7e8946-b8bd-5c22-9ef3-b4fcc20d9ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$24$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d104f5d3-66ed-5d0f-978b-7632a7a40047" :answer-field/id #uuid "d104f5d3-66ed-5d0f-978b-7632a7a40047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["fa9bf1a9-9ed3-510e-8652-4bea14db43c6" "08f23811-b1ee-5151-b6b6-f608a52a57d3" "87ffd388-fbdd-5be1-b220-e00d63314682" "90fa38bd-a1a3-5389-bd58-781b51e91810" "cf7e8946-b8bd-5c22-9ef3-b4fcc20d9ffb"] :answer-field/correct "90fa38bd-a1a3-5389-bd58-781b51e91810" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d1c8cfbb-47f4-5fb3-a9b0-9087d81918f8" :question/id #uuid "d1c8cfbb-47f4-5fb3-a9b0-9087d81918f8" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=50t e^{-0.1t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=80+20\\sin(2\\pi t/2)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $8\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(510-480)/60=0.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(0.5)-C(0.5) & =50(0.5){e}^{-0.1(0.5)}-(80+20\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{2}(0.5))) \\\\  & =50(0.5){e}^{-0.05}-80-20\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =50(0.5){e}^{-0.05}-100 \\\\  & \\approx -76.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $-76$ cars per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["d104f5d3-66ed-5d0f-978b-7632a7a40047"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "b03e3130-ebeb-56a0-a735-21aa477c71ae" :answer/id #uuid "b03e3130-ebeb-56a0-a735-21aa477c71ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$156$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" :answer/id #uuid "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$121$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "48c1409d-fc69-54ea-b9a0-2713986d307a" :answer/id #uuid "48c1409d-fc69-54ea-b9a0-2713986d307a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-35$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "de1c0611-7856-5339-b7b2-d83aedf32026" :answer/id #uuid "de1c0611-7856-5339-b7b2-d83aedf32026" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$191$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2b6c992b-a9bf-50ec-a63b-953cb1055324" :answer/id #uuid "2b6c992b-a9bf-50ec-a63b-953cb1055324" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-121$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9a42ed69-259b-5d9d-b5a0-92f539029c30" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a42ed69-259b-5d9d-b5a0-92f539029c30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["b03e3130-ebeb-56a0-a735-21aa477c71ae" "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" "48c1409d-fc69-54ea-b9a0-2713986d307a" "de1c0611-7856-5339-b7b2-d83aedf32026" "2b6c992b-a9bf-50ec-a63b-953cb1055324"] :answer-field/correct "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "bd6eb95d-7375-5343-986b-68f30ad5b2d2" :question/id #uuid "bd6eb95d-7375-5343-986b-68f30ad5b2d2" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=90t e^{-0.2t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=20+15\\sin(2\\pi t/14)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $11\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(690-480)/60=3.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(3.5)-C(3.5) & =90(3.5){e}^{-0.2(3.5)}-(20+15\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{14}(3.5))) \\\\  & =90(3.5){e}^{-0.7}-20-15\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =90(3.5){e}^{-0.7}-35 \\\\  & \\approx 121.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $121$ cars per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["9a42ed69-259b-5d9d-b5a0-92f539029c30"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "b20f23c0-8c87-5d2b-ba53-496addf07a38" :answer/id #uuid "b20f23c0-8c87-5d2b-ba53-496addf07a38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$69$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e224aaed-7ace-5ee6-9efa-77876f3b74e2" :answer/id #uuid "e224aaed-7ace-5ee6-9efa-77876f3b74e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-69$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6de37857-a139-5858-9e56-fc09b996a51d" :answer/id #uuid "6de37857-a139-5858-9e56-fc09b996a51d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$129$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "088dec50-c3c6-50e5-9b69-0e7ce15be0f8" :answer/id #uuid "088dec50-c3c6-50e5-9b69-0e7ce15be0f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-60$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e2822869-04a9-5b0d-8a9d-94e5390e105e" :answer/id #uuid "e2822869-04a9-5b0d-8a9d-94e5390e105e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$189$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5c87e9ae-3f6c-51f1-aa5d-040dc2bf3415" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c87e9ae-3f6c-51f1-aa5d-040dc2bf3415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["b20f23c0-8c87-5d2b-ba53-496addf07a38" "e224aaed-7ace-5ee6-9efa-77876f3b74e2" "6de37857-a139-5858-9e56-fc09b996a51d" "088dec50-c3c6-50e5-9b69-0e7ce15be0f8" "e2822869-04a9-5b0d-8a9d-94e5390e105e"] :answer-field/correct "b20f23c0-8c87-5d2b-ba53-496addf07a38" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "f2e135c6-4cc0-5a93-bc48-e0df9714cad2" :question/id #uuid "f2e135c6-4cc0-5a93-bc48-e0df9714cad2" :question/problem "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=100t e^{-0.1t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=40+20\\sin(2\\pi t/6)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $9\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(570-480)/60=1.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(1.5)-C(1.5) & =100(1.5){e}^{-0.1(1.5)}-(40+20\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}(1.5))) \\\\  & =100(1.5){e}^{-0.15}-40-20\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =100(1.5){e}^{-0.15}-60 \\\\  & \\approx 69.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $69$ cars per hour." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["5c87e9ae-3f6c-51f1-aa5d-040dc2bf3415"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "cc796484-ad70-51d7-bb01-5b8342bff754" :answer/id #uuid "cc796484-ad70-51d7-bb01-5b8342bff754" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$180$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d16bf7d6-ca47-5047-90d1-e323cc45a658" :answer/id #uuid "d16bf7d6-ca47-5047-90d1-e323cc45a658" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$105$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b937214f-6d30-5777-98d4-63d7c6dc1a65" :answer/id #uuid "b937214f-6d30-5777-98d4-63d7c6dc1a65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-105$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ba2e00ae-4e6a-5d71-aef7-bdb151691a73" :answer/id #uuid "ba2e00ae-4e6a-5d71-aef7-bdb151691a73" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-75$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "26ada36c-1091-5f42-8c63-eccc8b641f55" :answer/id #uuid "26ada36c-1091-5f42-8c63-eccc8b641f55" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$255$ cars per hour" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "60